# Semantic HTML page blueprint

When building or editing a page, use this landmark structure. Project extras (`id="body"`, `<!-- include:header.html -->`, `<!-- include:footer.html -->`, `data-role`) sit **on** this tree — they do not replace it.

```
body
  header            page chrome (logo + nav)
    nav > ul > li > a
  main
    section#…       one thematic block; heading is h1 then h2…
      article       one self-contained piece
        header      title + meta
          h3
          p > time[datetime]
        p           body copy
        footer      article meta (tags, updated)
  footer            page chrome
```

## Rules

- Landmarks: one `header` / `nav` / `main` / page `footer`. Group related articles in `section`, not a bare `div`.
- Headings: do not skip levels. Page/section use `h1`/`h2`; article titles are `h3` inside `article > header`.
- Copy is `<p>`, dates are `<time datetime="YYYY-MM-DD">`. Do not use `<div>` for paragraphs or `<sub>`/`<sup>` as metadata.
- `article > footer` is article meta only; it is not the page footer.
- IDs are unique. Prefer `section` ids for in-page nav (`#home`, `#blog`).
- Allowed extras that do not break the tree: `figure`/`img` for media, `dl` for key/value, `ul`/`span.tag` for tags **inside** `article > footer`.
